$
.title	AMY1 version 3 including host sync modifications
$
$******************************************************************************
$
$ This file is a hand edited version of the net list extracted from the
$ AMY1 Daisy drawings in about October 1984.  The edits are as follows:
$
$ (-1)	The string "$/USER/BOB/AMY/" was replaced by "$ " to shorten the
$ file and bring a little more meaningful portion of the comment field
$ into view.
$
$  (0)	This file has had all occurances of vcc replaced by .vcc
$ and gnd replaced by .gnd
$ to take advantage of SILOS automatic definition and anticipated
$ updates to SILOS that will make certain substitution of resistive
$ uni-directional functions for bi-directionals controlled by supplies.
$
$  (1)	Lines like  " xyz .nmos .vcc martha ralph " were used for pullups and
$ SILOS thinks such things are shorts from ralph to martha.  These were
$ replaced by " ralph .res martha ".
$
$  (2)	Initialization of some nodes in the divide-by-2 clock circuitry
$ was necessary otherwise the clock was locked up in a ring of "unknowns".
$
$  (3)	A three input nor gate generating v7 at the outputs of the voice
$ counter was improperly drawn on the DAISY and generated a bad net list
$ but Ben Calpo has checked the IC layout and determined that a nor gate
$ was built.  I have edited in the corresponding conditions on v7 here.
$
$  (4)	A special version of the counter cell was used for the
$ voice counter to prevent oscillation from feed-back designed to
$ stop the counter at its max count value.
$
$  (5)	The resistive pullups on the phase ram outputs, phdb0..phdb19, were
$ removed because SILOS apparently implements .RAM outputs with "resistive"
$ strength.  Ben Calpo has looked at the ram output timing and feels that
$ this modification of the net list will not mask a problem.  To compensate,
$ where the phase RAM inputs are being driven I had to put in a modified
$ macro "TRIHpu" which includes a pullup gated on by the enable.
$ The same fix was applied to the hbus to/from the harmonic ram.
$
$  (6)	A reset was added to the ZEROB flip flop.
$
$  (7)	The names "HADRE?" were changed to "hadr?n" where ?=0..5 to conform
$ to the naming convention with "n" for negated signals and to conform with
$ the Daisy drawings and Ben Calpo's drawings.
$
$  (8)	An OR gate was inserted into the lines from CNT0 and CNT1 counter
$ bit cells to the P0..P3 decoder so that the system would be in state P0
$ during the RESET period and would spend only one clock time in each P-time
$ thereafter.  The earlier version held itself in P1 during RESET and spent
$ two P-times in P1 after the RST signal became inactive.  This resulted in
$ a failure to initialize the phase of voice zero's oscillator.
$
$  (9)	The comparitor cell was modified in the companion macro file to avoid
$ feedback when one of the inputs is "unknown".
$
$******************************************************************************
$
$ Initialize some nodes in the divide-by-2 clock ring.
$
.init	x192k19=0
$******************************************************************************
$ Build modifications to synchronize host communications
xx1		.or/n	rdha d2 wrha	$ is a host request to hram present?
xxclkn		.nmos	clkn p1 xx2	$ generate 2nd half p1 pulse
xx3		.nand/n	xx1 xx2		$ may go low during last half of p1
xxclk		.nmos	clk xx4 xx3	$ sample at beginning of p2
p2y		.inv/n	xx4		$ high during p2 if hram request
$
xy1		.or/n	wrff wrffnz
xy2		.and	p3 xy1
$
